# Commit and branch conventions

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) for branch names, commit messages, and pull request titles.

- Branch: `<type>/<short-description>` in kebab-case. Example: `fix/contact-email-overflow`.
- Title: `<type>: <imperative summary>`. Example: `fix: keep the contact email inside its card`.
- Use `feat` for a new capability, `fix` for a bug, and `chore` for maintenance that does not change site behavior.
- Do not use `bug`, `bugfix`, `feature`, `features`, or `bugs` as the type.
- Keep the title to one line. Do not append a pull request number.
